From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] mach_loader: let process 1 be a static executable on SBSA

A RELEASE kernel refuses every static arm64 executable (MH_EXECUTE without
MH_DYLDLINK) with LOAD_FAILURE; only DEVELOPMENT and DEBUG kernels load
them. NeoDarwin's first userland runs before the system has dyld: mockfs
roots on one static executable and runs it as /sbin/launchd (P1-07), and
the bring-up design allows a static init shim until launchd arrives
(docs/kernel/arm64-sbsa-bringup.md §2.4). Found as EXEC_EXIT_REASON_BAD_MACHO
at the first mockfs exec.

For GENERIC_ARM64_PLATFORM only, the executable itself (depth 1) may be
static when its task is process 1. Whoever supplies /sbin/launchd on the
root already controls the system, so this grants nothing new; every other
process keeps Apple's rule, and other board configs are unchanged.

Rebase-risk: low (one branch in parse_machfile).
---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c b/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c
--- a/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c
@@ -74,6 +74,9 @@
 #include <kern/mach_fat.h>
 #include <kern/kalloc.h>
 #include <kern/task.h>
+#if defined(__arm64__)
+#include <pexpert/arm64/board_config.h>
+#endif
 #include <kern/thread.h>
 #include <kern/page_decrypt.h>
 
@@ -1149,6 +1152,15 @@
 		} else if (imgp->ip_flags & IMGPF_ROSETTA) {
 			/* Rosetta runtime allowed */
 #endif /* CONFIG_X86_64_COMPAT */
+#if GENERIC_ARM64_PLATFORM
+		} else if (depth == 1 && thread != THREAD_NULL &&
+		    task_pid(get_threadtask(thread)) == 1) {
+			/*
+			 * NeoDarwin: process 1 may be static. It runs before a system has dyld
+			 * (mockfs's executable, the init shim), and whoever supplies /sbin/launchd
+			 * already controls the system; every other static executable is refused.
+			 */
+#endif
 		} else {
 			/* Check properties of static executables (disallowed except for development) */
 #if !(DEVELOPMENT || DEBUG)
